==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|orv|игра}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*jьgra}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|игра́}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-игра.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|d|игра́|adj=иго́рный,игрово́й|hypocor=игру́ля|pej=игрёшка|expr=игру́ха,игрёха}}

# [[game]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''игра́''' [[в]] [[мяч]]|ball game}}
# a [[sport]] which is played (''also'' {{m|ru|[[спортивный|спорти́вная]] игра́}})
# ''(action)'': [[play]] in the following senses:
## Activity for amusement only, especially among the young.
## Similar activity, in young animals, as they explore their environment and learn new skills.
## {{lb|ru|ethology}} "Repeated, incompletely functional behavior differing from more serious versions ..., and initiated voluntarily when ... in a low-stress setting."
## An individual's performance in a sport or game.
# [[acting]], [[performance]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''игра́''' [[актёр|актёра]]|an actor’s performance}}
# [[role-playing]] (''also'' {{m|ru|[[ролевой|ролева́я]] игра́}})
# [[playing]] ''(a musical instrument)''
#: {{uxi|ru|'''игра́''' [[на]] [[гитара|гита́ре]]|playing the [[guitar]]}}
# [[movement]] of [[gas]] [[bubbles]] in a [[sparkling]] drink
# {{lb|ru|figuratively}} [[glitter]], [[sparkle]], [[radiance]] (of precious stones)

